      "extract": "Let $M=(m_{ij})$ be a symmetric $n\\times n$ matrix over natural numbers, with $\\infty$ such that $m_{ii}=1,2\\leq m_{ij}\\leq \\infty$ for $i\\ne j$. The matrix $M$ determines a group with the following presentation $$W=\\mbox{sgp}\\langle s_1,..,s_n|(s_is_j)^{m_{ij}}=1, \\mbox{ where } 1\\leq i,j\\leq n, m_{ij}\\ne \\infty\\rangle,$$ which is called the Coxeter group $W=W(M)$. The study of Coxeter groups can be said to go back",
      "extractCut": true
    },
